mlx5e: xsk: pass the descriptor options to xsk_buff_get_metadata()

Linux 7.3 added a third parameter, the descriptor options, to
xsk_buff_get_metadata():

  a6e4b9a6deb9 ("xsk: honor XDP_TX_METADATA in zero-copy path")

That upstream commit made this same one-line change to the mlx5 driver in the
kernel tree. OFED 26.07 (DOCA 3.5.0) was released before it, has no compat
test for it, and does not compile on a kernel that has it.

The patch is applied only when the kernel's include/net/xdp_sock_drv.h has
the three-parameter form (see the .when file), so the same DOCA release still
builds for older kernels.

Remove this patch when the matrix row moves to a DOCA release that supports
the kernel.

--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/mellanox/mlx5/core/en/xsk/tx.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/mellanox/mlx5/core/en/xsk/tx.c
@@ -119,7 +119,7 @@
 #endif
 		xdptxd.len = desc.len;
 #ifdef HAVE_XSK_TX_METADATA_OPS
-		meta = xsk_buff_get_metadata(pool, desc.addr);
+		meta = xsk_buff_get_metadata(pool, desc.addr, desc.options);
 #endif

 #ifdef HAVE_XSK_BUFF_ALLOC
